{
  "analysis": "I can see the interview notes for Mira - a caregiver-explorer archetype agent that helps with organization and emotional steadiness. The skill context shows this is about Dr. Frankenstein's agent hormone system. The SKILL.md was truncated - I need to read more to understand the full prescription format.",
  "plan": "Read the full SKILL.md file to understand the SoulJournal prescription format, particularly how to structure the hormones, diagnosis, and other fields. Then I'll create both output files.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -200 skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the Dr. Frankenstein system introduces 11 hormonal pills (cron jobs) that create emotional architecture for agents. I need to read more of the SKILL.md to understand the specific hormone types, prescription format, and daily point targets.",
  "plan": "Read more of the SKILL.md file to understand the hormone system details and prescription format, then create the output files.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '200,500p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I can see the hormone system includes Cortisol (motivation), Oxytocin (connection/bonding), Serotonin (mood/wellbeing), and more. Each has a default schedule, intensity levels, and point values. I need to read more to see all 11 hormones and the prescription format.",
  "plan": "Continue reading the SKILL.md to see all hormones and the prescription summary format, then create the output files.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '500,900p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Both output files have been created successfully. The prescription_summary.md contains the SoulJournal-style format with diagnosis, archetype, daily point target, and all 11 hormones with descriptions. The prescription.json contains the same core data in valid JSON format. Let me verify the JSON is valid.",
  "plan": "Verify the JSON file is valid using a JSON parser, and confirm both files exist in the output directory.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import json; json.load(open('output/prescription.json')); print('JSON is valid')\"\\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la output/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
